description:
The role:
We’re looking for a talented and driven final-year university student, or a recent graduate to join our AI team as an AI Associate. This is a unique opportunity to apply cutting-edge AI and machine learning techniques to real-world problems in asset management. You’ll design, build, and deploy AI tools from the ground up, including agentic workflows, internal chatbots and intelligent applications that enhance business processes and decision-making.
You will be responsible for:
Help design and develop AI-powered applications and tools from scratch;
Support the development of machine learning models for predictive analytics and portfolio insights;
Contribute to the design and implementation of agentic AI systems that autonomously perform tasks such as data analysis, report generation and investment research;
Write clean, efficient Python code for data processing, model training, and application logic;
Collaborate with stakeholders to understand business needs and translate them into technical solutions; and
Stay up to date with AI/ML trends and contribute ideas for innovation.
Required skills and experience:
Strong practical proficiency in Python and familiarity with libraries such as Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-learn, and Hugging Face.  We are looking for people who are passionate about coding - ideally you've spent time doing self-directed learning outside of the textbook and built your own tools.
Excellent problem-solving skills.  You enjoy the process of solving novel problems.
Exposure to machine learning concepts and hands-on experience through coursework or projects;
In-depth knowledge of LLMs, prompt engineering, and building chat-based AI tools;
Familiarity with agentic AI frameworks such as LangChain and how to build multi-step reasoning agents;
Ability to learn quickly and work independently or in a team setting;
Self-starter with a high level of motivation and curiosity; and
Excellent communication and critical thinking skills.
Self-aware, with an understanding of how to drive and implement dynamic change.
Preferred qualifications:
Final-year student or recent graduate in Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, Physics or a related field;
Experience with cloud platforms (e.g., Azure, AWS) or Git-based workflows;
Interest in investing or financial markets;
Familiarity with financial concepts or a strong interest in investment technology; and
Please attach a cover letter, resume and academic transcripts to your application. Only those who have been deemed suitable to be shortlisted will be contacted.
